-----> create a pod  <-----------
create pod.yml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: mypod
spec:
  containers:
    - name: cont-1
      image: sree978/sree/appv1
      ports:
        - containerPort: 80
kubectl create -f pod.yml    to create pods 

Kubectl get po    - to get pods
Kubectl describe pod podname    to check labels

kubectl get po --show-labels    to get labels from multiple pods


if we want labels will give to metadata in manifest file 
we can add labels for existed pods also
kubectl label pod podname "env=test"
or 
kubectl label pod mypod app=nginx env=dev version=v1 department=testing

-------------> Labels  <--------------------

Labels:

Labels are used to organize Kubernetes Objects such as Pods, nodes, etc.
You can add multiple labels over the Kubernetes Objects.
Labels are defined in key-value pairs.
Labels are similar to tags in AWS or Azure where you give a name to filter the resources quickly.
You can add labels like environment, department or anything else according to you.
  

